<i>b</i>, significat 30 et 6 , 5 sibi substitui posse. Ut <i>hominem</i> et\n[[144.21]] <i>animal rationale</i>. </p>\n<p> [[144.22]] <i>a</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>a</i>. <i>Homo est homo</i>. Patet per se. </p>\n<p> [[144.23]] Si <i>a</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i> et <i>b</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>c</i> erit <i>a</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>c</i>, patet ex significatione ipsius ^&.zg <Leibniz special character>. </p>\n<p> [[145.1]] <i>c</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>d</i> significat <i>d</i> substitui posse in locum ipsius <i>c</i>. Idem significat etiam <i>d</i> ^&.zd <Leibniz special character> <i>c</i>. Ut si\n[[145.2]] <i>c</i> sit <i>homo</i> <i>d</i> sit <i>animal</i> vulgo sic enuntiatur <i>Homo est animal</i>. </p>\n<p> [[145.3]] <i>c</i> ^&.ze <Leibniz special character> <i>d</i> significat <i>d</i> substitui posse in locum ipsius [<i>c</i>] sed non contra. </p>\n<p> [[145.4]] Hinc si <i>c</i> ^&.ze <Leibniz special character> <i>d</i> erit <i>c</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>d</i> et <i>d non</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>c</i>. </p>\n<p> [[145.5]] Si <i>c non</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>d</i> et <i>c non</i> ^&.ze <Leibniz special character> <i>d</i> erit <i>c non</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>d</i>. </p>\n<p> [[145.6]] Si <i>a</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i> erit <i>a</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i> et <i>b</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>a</i>, et erit <i>a non</i> ^&.ze <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i> et <i>b non</i> ^&.ze <Leibniz special character> <i>a</i>. </p>\n<p> [[145.7]] Contra si <i>a</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i> et <i>b</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>a</i> erit <i>a</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i>. </p>\n<p> [[145.8]] Si <i>a</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i> et <i>b</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>c</i>, erit [<i>a</i>] ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>c</i>, ut si <i>homo sit animal</i> et <i>animal sit</i> <i>substantia</i>, <i>homo erit\n[[145.9]] substantia</i>. </p>\n<p> [[145.10]] <i>bc</i>, significat si <i>a</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>bc</i> erit <i>a</i> ^&.ze <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i> et erit <i>a</i> ^&.ze <Leibniz special character> <i>c</i>. </p>\n<p> [[145.11]] Hinc si <i>d</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>bc</i> erit <i>d</i> ^&.ze <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i> et <i>d</i> ^&.ze <Leibniz special character> <i>c</i>. </p>\n<p> [[145.12]] Si <i>a</i> ^&.ze <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i> erit <i>a</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>by</i>. </p>\n<p> [[145.13]] Si <i>a non</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>by</i> et <i>a non</i> ^&.zg <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i> erit <i>a non</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> <i>b</i>. </p>\n",
